---
title: Open and save selected documents
description: Read a document, save a copy and browse one selected folder without native paths.
---

<span hidden data-pagefind-filter="SDK:preview.3 candidate"></span>

**Unreleased preview.3 candidate.** These APIs are absent from the published
preview.2 SDK. Keep its released declarations and packages unchanged. There is
no new public SDK download on this page.

Use the optional `@LuiWorkbench/Files` module for documents the user selects.

Use `File:ByteLength(Callback)` for the current byte length and `File:ReadRange(Position, Count, Callback)` to process a large document incrementally. Position is zero-based. Count is 1–65,536. The callback receives a buffer and an optional failure code. Offsets at or beyond EOF produce an empty buffer. A file may change between reads. The headless `file-summary` SDK example accepts an operator-selected file through `--read-file`.
For uncommitted writes to a selected save destination, use `File:BeginWriter(Callback)`. Its seekable writer accepts 64 KiB chunks, up to 128 MiB per draft. `Commit` replaces the destination; `Close` discards an unfinished draft. See the packaged `atomic-copy` example.

A headless host can fulfill OpenFolder with an explicitly writable directory using `--write-directory DIRECTORY`. Use `Folder:OpenOutput`, `CreateDirectory`, `RemoveFile`, `RemoveDirectory` (empty only) and `Rename(From, To, Callback)` for direct children. Rename refuses an existing destination. The `--read-directory` grant and desktop folder pickers expose reads and listing. `Files.Copy(Source, Destination, Callback)` streams 64 KiB at a time and publishes the replacement on commit. Closing either file ends the copy. Disposing either picker cancels it. See the candidate's `folder-copy` project.

For sequential work, create a cursor with `Files.Reader(File, Offset?)`. Each successful `Reader:Read(Count, Callback)` advances its position by the delivered length. `Reader:Position()` and `Reader:Seek(Offset)` use zero-based byte offsets. Canceling a pending read preserves its starting position. Close each cursor, then close the file when all readers finish.

Use Preferences for app-private settings or a scratchpad. The two grants serve
different purposes; a native path string from preview.2's legacy picker does not
grant filesystem access.

The complete candidate `Examples/selected-files` project includes its vendor
files, module lock and `Dialogs` capability. Copy the whole folder outside the
SDK, then run `lui check` and `lui run --mode project` with that candidate SDK.
The native WinUI3/GTK4.10+ host needs a visible parent window for a picker.
Ordinary apps need no C++ code, provider registration or native file paths.

